{{also|erde}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|erda}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*erþō}}. Compare {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|aarde}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|ierde}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|earth}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|jord}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌸𐌰}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʔeːɐ̯də/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|de-Erde.ogg|audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|eːɐ̯də|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|Erde|Erden}}

# the planet [[Earth]]
# [[soil]]
#: {{ux|de|Sie nahm eine Handvoll '''Erde'''.|t=She took a handful of soil.|inline=1}}
# the [[ground]]
#: {{ux|de|Er fiel auf die '''Erde'''.|t=He fell on the ground.|inline=1}}

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-f|n|n}}

====Usage notes====
The old dative form {{m|de|Erden}} is only used in the phrase {{m|de|auf Erden}} ("on earth"), which has a religious or solemn ring to it. In most contexts it is preferable to say ''auf der Erde''.

